Whether a number is even, with even and odd defined in terms of each other. Written the natural way, with the letrecs nested, odd is not in scope where even is defined.
The probe is mutual recursion: the language has self-recursion through letrec, but no way to bind two functions that call each other.
---
(lam n
  (letrec even (lam k (if (= k 0) 1 (odd (- k 1))))
    (letrec odd (lam k (if (= k 0) 0 (even (- k 1))))
      (even n))))
---
0 => 1 fuel 10000
4 => 1 fuel 10000
7 => 0 fuel 10000
